Evidence for That Open — the app channel's two servers do not share rooms
Measured 2026-09-29 (UTC) on Windows 11 with WebApp/scripts/thatopen-channel-repro.mjs (node v26.5.0, socket.io-client 4.8.3).
The listener is a real app tab: the published Sentinel app open in Chrome on platform.thatopen.com (project and app ids below).
The asker publishes one command (sentinel.status, which the app answers) through a socket pinned to one server address.
'publish ack' is the platform's own acknowledgement; 'app replied' means the app's answer came back.
No token appears in this file.

